The servicing app's transfer-batch codec and its 1.1 data-quality gate
(spec §1.1), ported for the life generator's transfer-package writer and the
boarding-triage environment.

Source       apps/servicing/src/domain/boarding/{tape-codec,rules,min}.ts
Vendored at  293261b371fe97d2b6b39e1f29ca60dd808ac8fb (apps/servicing/VENDORED_FROM)
Ported       2026-10-23

Each file here is its source byte for byte except its import statements,
and the rewrite is three rules and no more:
  - the kernel's paths (../../kernel/{calendar,money}/<file>.ts) become
    @hm/kernel/{calendar,money} (the same bytes; packages/kernel/VENDORED_FROM);
  - ./types.ts becomes ../../pmi/ported/types.js. The boarding types are
    already ported, byte for byte, for the pmi-termination environment, and
    held there (src/pmi/ported/PORTED_FROM); one copy, not two;
  - a sibling's ./<file>.ts becomes ./<file>.js.
Nothing else may be edited: src/__tests__/boarding.test.ts rewrites each
original's imports by these rules, compares, and compares the rest of each
file, and fails on any difference. Lint and Prettier skip this directory for
the reason they skip the vendored trees.

No file the port needs is ours.

What each is for. The writer encodes every package through
`encodeTransferBatch`, so a package is laid out exactly as the sample batch
is (apps/servicing/fixtures/transfer-batch-demo/) and reads back through the
decoder the servicing app boards with. The environment's generator runs the
gate's own rules (`runRules`) over every package, planted or clean, and keeps
only one on whose every loan all thirty-five pass, so what is left for the
model to find is what the gate cannot see. The code-list tool reads the
final tape's column dictionary (`FINAL_TAPE_COLUMNS`), and a test holds the
detail files' columns to the codec's headers.

Not ported: service.ts (the stateful boarding service, which imports the
event store, the ledger and the transfers modules), delinquency.ts (already
ported for pmi-termination), demo-batch.ts and fixtures.ts (the sample's
generator and the test harness). apps/servicing/scripts/board-life-package.mjs
runs the servicing app's own service, in process, over a written package.

To take a change from the servicing app, copy the three files again and apply
the same three rewrites.
